# SABOTAGE: D-01 (operator ruling, 2026-09-09) — THE ERASURE REPORT'S DERIVED-SUMMARY
# DISCLOSURE IS DROPPED. The `:shredded` clauses of `derived_summary_invalidation/1` and
# `derived_summary_reason/1` are rewritten to the CLEAN-PATH answer, so a report written
# after a `{:error, :shredded}` STEP 0 pseudonym read claims `"invalidation" => "performed"`
# with a `null` reason — byte-identical to a report written after a genuinely clean
# derived-summary invalidation. The subject's derived AI summaries survive un-invalidated
# and NOTHING says so: not the report tier, not the STEP 4a audit detail, not the STEP 4b
# AuditChain detail (all three read the same function). That is the repo's own fail-honest
# lie (ADR-014/024/026, `CLAUDE.md`: "an adapter NEVER returns {:ok, _} for work it did not
# do") wearing an erasure hat, and it is exactly what D-01 forbids.
#
# WHAT STAYS GREEN UNDER THIS PATCH — the proof the red fires for the RIGHT reason:
#   * `D-01 ANTI-TAUTOLOGY` (the `:performed` clauses are untouched),
#   * `D-01 IDEMPOTENCY` and every shipped `C4I1` arm — CARVE-OUT `:shredded`, CARVE-OUT
#     `:absent`, FAIL-CLOSED + its positive control, ORDER + its positive control.
# Erasure still PROCEEDS, stays IDEMPOTENT, and stays FAIL-CLOSED: this patch changes only
# what the run SAYS, never what it DOES. Compiles clean under `--warnings-as-errors` (two
# literal clause bodies swap; no clause is deleted, so no head becomes unreachable and no
# variable becomes unused). Touches `samen_core/lib/samen/erasure.ex` ALONE.
#
# Authored by D1I against its OWN built code, not lifted from D1R's `D01.planned.patch`
# (which anchored on a different shape and could not apply).
